<main class="zd-philosophy-page">

  <section class="zd-philosophy-hero">
    <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">Philosophy</p>

    <h1>Technology should serve your life, not steal it.</h1>

    <p>
      Ziyu Development is built around one belief: software should help people
      become more focused, intentional, capable, and present in real life.
    </p>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-actions">
      <a href="/pages/projects" class="zd-philosophy-btn zd-philosophy-btn--primary">Explore Projects</a>
      <a href="/pages/support" class="zd-philosophy-btn zd-philosophy-btn--secondary">Support the Mission</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-split">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">What is broken</p>
      <h2>Modern technology often rewards distraction.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-text">
      <p>
        Many apps are designed to increase time spent, not life improved.
        They pull attention into feeds, notifications, streaks, and algorithms
        that keep people consuming instead of becoming.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ziyu Development exists to build the opposite: tools that support focus,
        growth, learning, reflection, and meaningful action.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-principles">
    <div class="zd-philosophy-section-head">
      <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">Core principles</p>
      <h2>The beliefs behind every project.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-grid">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Focus Over Noise</h3>
        <p>
          Tools should protect attention and help people spend their time on what matters.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Real-Life Growth</h3>
        <p>
          Apps should support habits, learning, relationships, work, and personal progress.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Clean Information</h3>
        <p>
          People need better ways to find books, ideas, and resources that build them up.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Human Technology</h3>
        <p>
          Software should feel calm, useful, respectful, and designed for actual humans.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>05</span>
        <h3>Intentional Design</h3>
        <p>
          Every feature, page, product, and interaction should have a clear purpose.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>06</span>
        <h3>Build in Public</h3>
        <p>
          Progress should be visible so supporters can trust what is being created.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-products">
    <div>
      <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">How it becomes real</p>
      <h2>Each product solves a different part of the same problem.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="zd-philosophy-product-list">
      <a href="/pages/goal-grower">
        <strong>Goal Grower</strong>
        <span>Growth, goals, habits, accountability.</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/myjourney">
        <strong>MyJourney</strong>
        <span>Reflection, planning, life direction.</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/blokkr">
        <strong>Blokkr</strong>
        <span>Focus, attention, distraction blocking.</span>
      </a>

      <a href="/pages/kindlitt">
        <strong>Kindlitt</strong>
        <span>Reading, clean information, better discovery.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="zd-philosophy-vision">
    <p class="zd-philosophy-eyebrow">The future</p>

    <h2>A complete ecosystem for intentional living.</h2>

    <p>
      The long-term vision is not just one app. It is a connected ecosystem of
      software, physical products, writing, and community that helps people
      build better lives with more focus, clarity, and purpose.
    </p>

    <a href="/pages/roadmap" class="zd-philosophy-btn zd-philosophy-btn--light">View the Roadmap</a>
  </section>

</main>

